-## Selection policy
-
-- Main (best compression on repeatedly used human development samples): `234`.
-- Balanced alternative (weaker penalty on random-legal controls): `231`.
-- Previous checkpoints: `182` and `119`, left intact.
-- Production readiness: **research only**; generalization and 60–70K plies/s speed target are not met.
-
-## Usage
-
-```bash
-cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
-cmake --build build --target dmg_mid dmt_default_tests dmt10_tests -j4
-./build/dmg_mid main
-./build/dmg_mid pack result.dmt examples/heldout/*.uci               # default 234
-./build/dmg_mid pack default result.dmt examples/heldout/*.uci       # explicit default alias
-./build/dmg_mid pack r10-combo-tact4-full result.dmt examples/heldout/*.uci
-./build/dmg_mid pack r10-combo-tact2-mix result.dmt examples/heldout/*.uci  # 231
-./build/dmg_mid unpack result.dmt /tmp/recovered
-ctest --test-dir build -R 'dmt_default_profile|dmt10_focused_roundtrip' --output-on-failure
-```
-
-Compatibility: an omitted profile in `pack` is only accepted if the archive filename ends in `.dmt`; unknown profile strings cause an error, never a silent fallback.
-
-For research comparisons pass explicit numeric IDs to `dmt9_experiments`; default selection must not confound historical results.
-
-## 2026-10-22 output-preserving optimization and DMT11 experiments
-
-See `README-R11.md`. Default remains 234. IDs 243–248 are isolated DMTB research candidates, not promoted defaults. `reference-dmt10/` contains the immutable source baseline used in comparisons.
+- 42 probability configurations explored; 50 new games for development, 25 for selection, 25 held out until the preset was frozen.
+- Existing IDs 0–248 remain byte-compatible. New configurable stream: DMTC/249; fixed preset: DMTD/250.
+- Normal build enables exact feature-score tables; opportunity-node cache is experimental and OFF.
+- LTO is optional; PGO was tested and is not a default recommendation.
+- Research only: no claim that all phase compression or 60–70K speed targets are met.
